// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue - FortunataSybil 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue Name :
"P3886062731" "Fortunata Bramlett"
// DetailString :
"P3125779089" "You rescued Fortunata Bramlett from Longbow, and she was more than willing to repay your work by agreeing to Sister Airlia's plan. Now you just need to get her to the Sybil temple."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue - CimonLocation 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue Name :
"P6778282" "Cimon's New Headquarters"
// DetailString :
"P3066271499" "Captain Cimon was quick to take advantage of your elimination of his enemies. He's set up his headquarters in a nearby cave. While it is well guarded, it is also sheltered from any prying eyes, making your upcoming task all the more easy to conceal."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue - CreyBase 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue Name :
"P2431587798" "Crey Warehouse Location"
// DetailString :
"P2436112168" "Why can't anything ever be easy? At least Darrin Wade gave you the location of the warehouse you hit to get the artifact to trade for the Aquila sword."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue - MysteriousArtifact 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue Name :
"P13299559" "Mysterious Artifact"
// DetailString :
"P1977873391" "It's doesn't look like much but it must have something going for it, to get Crey and the Family so interested in it. But it's not your problem; you just need to deliver it to Darrin Wade and get your hands on the Aquila sword."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue - AquilaSword 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue Name :
"P2773052505" "Aquila Family Sword"
// DetailString :
"P3299286462" "This ancient blade is in surprisingly good shape for something this old. You hope Senator Aquila appreciates it after all of the trouble you've went to to get your hands on it."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue - TaintedUrn 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue Name :
"P678087622" "Ancient Urn"
// DetailString :
"P3547173932" "This ancient urn has been modified by Sister Airlia with an enchantment just for Imperious. You'll deliver it to him after you help save him during a battle. Working for someone who can see the future has its advantages; you know what you'll be doing in advance."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue - Mission1Clue 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue Name :
"P3865887481" "Politics, Cimeroran Style"
// DetailString :
"P4232314347" "Sister Airlia hired you to convince a Fortunata to come work for her and pose as a Sybil in Cimerora. Recruiting the Sybil was easy -- you just had to rescue her from her Longbow captors first. Things got interesting when you returned to Cimerora. The Sybil temple was under attack and you used the opportunity to slip the disguised Fortunata into the area. Of course, you had to bust some Roman heads to make sure they wouldn't overrun the temple, but that was all in a day's work."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue - Mission2Clue 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DetailString :
"P4246936094" "Sister Airlia hired you to convince a Fortunata to come work for her and pose as a Sybil in Cimerora. Recruiting the Sybil was easy -- you just had to rescue her from her Longbow captors first. Things got interesting when you returned to Cimerora. The Sybil temple was under attack and you used the opportunity to slip the disguised Fortunata into the area. Of course, you had to bust some Roman heads to make sure they wouldn't overrun the temple, but that was all in a day's work.<br><br>Sister Airlia's plan continued to unfold as she next had you beat up on some of Imperious' Roman traitors in the area. This caused Captain Cimon to see an opening and move his headquarters to a forward position. That made it all the more easy for you to go in there and eliminate Cimon and his men, which had its intended effect of shaking Imperious' faith in his military and making him more reliant on advice from the Sybils."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue - Mission3Clue 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DetailString :
"P3202400407" "Sister Airlia hired you to convince a Fortunata to come work for her and pose as a Sybil in Cimerora. Recruiting the Sybil was easy -- you just had to rescue her from her Longbow captors first. Things got interesting when you returned to Cimerora. The Sybil temple was under attack and you used the opportunity to slip the disguised Fortunata into the area. Of course, you had to bust some Roman heads to make sure they wouldn't overrun the temple, but that was all in a day's work.<br><br>Sister Airlia's plan continued to unfold as she next had you beat up on some of Imperious' Roman traitors in the area. This caused Captain Cimon to see an opening and move his headquarters to a forward position. That made it all the more easy for you to go in there and eliminate Cimon and his men, which had its intended effect of shaking Imperious' faith in his military and making him more reliant on advice from the Sybils.<br><br>Corrupting a politician is much easier in your time. But to bring Senator Aquila under her sway, Sister Airlia had you visit Darrin Wade in Sharkhead Isle to get Aquila's family sword, an heirloom that had been lost through the ages. Of course, Wade didn't just hand the sword over to you. He had you break into a Crey office where you interrupted Crey employees negotiating with representaives of The Family over a mysterious artifact. You entered the negotiations in your own unique way and, when the smoke cleared, left with the artifact in hand. You traded that back to Wade for the Aquila family sword and returned to Cimerora to present it to the good Senator with Sister Airlia's compliments. The Senator was duly thankful and promised to work on Sister Airlia's behalf."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// SouvenirClueDef - PoliticsCimeroranStyle 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// SouvenirClueDef Name :
"P3072533438" "An ancient urn"
// tDetailString :
"P4122661498" "This urn brings back memories of the caper you like to call:<br><br><color deepskyblue>Politics, Cimeroran Style</color><br><br> Sister Airlia enlisted your help to rearrange the power structure in Cimerora. First you visited the Rikti War Zone to enlist a Fortunata to come back to Cimerora with you and go into deep cover as a Sybil. Then you arranged for one of Imperious' Captains to disappear, weakening the military influece. A political restructuring wouldn't be complete without the chance to bribe a politician, and you had a chance to do just that when you arranged with Darrin Wade to recover Senator Aquila's family sword from the future and then used it to subvert him to Sister Airlia's cause. Finally you had the chance to deal with Imperious himself. You earned his gratitude by being the hero of a large battle and then handed him an enchanted urn that was designed to ensorcel him and make him pliable to Sister Airlia's advice. Sister Airlia is now well-positioned to infuence matters in Cimerora, making her a handy person to know."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task - Mission1 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Dialog - DialogTree 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Page Intro Text :
"P2149829398" "You have come as I had forseen, {VillainName}. Though I was in no danger from this paltry attack, I thank you for rescuing my sister from this danger.<br><br>You have done this Temple a great service and it embarrasses me to have to ask you to quit from this place, but that I must do. The violence of your aura disrupts the harmony of this place of peace. Please know that I hold no personal animosity for you and I hope that we can meet again under better circumstances."
// Answer Text :
"P4060782435" "Leave"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task Header Items 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// IntroString :
"P3608915352" "You <color orange>listen</color> to me, {VillainName}, and that's more than I can say for the narrow-minded fools here. They refuse to hear my visions, even though my guidance would greatly aid their struggles against their foes. No longer will I stand for this! With your help, I shall ensure that my voice will be <color orange>heard</color>.<br><br>Since those from your time seem intelligent enough to heed me, I would have you travel through time to visit the place you call Grandville and find one called <color orange>Fortunata Bramlett</color>. I have seen that she will be receptive to your approach. You will make her the offer to come with you to Cimerora, where she will assume the role of a Sybil and be my voice in Sister Solaris' ear.<br><br>When she accepts, bring her to the Sybil Temple. I see a dark cloud over it upon your return. Use that time of confusion to find Sister Solaris and deliver the new 'sister' to her."
// AcceptString :
"P3316371131" "Bring Fortunata Bramlett to Cimerora"
// SendOffString :
"P4238337094" "'Sister' Bramlett will ensure that Sister Solaris heeds my words and warnings. Through her, I shall be able to manipulate the Sybils."
// TaskTitle :
"P3866827391" "<color deepskyblue>Politics, Cimeroran Style</color>"
// TaskSubTitle :
"P2878948450" "<color deepskyblue>Part One: Going Deep Cover</color>"

